Search 4.9 million unique open jobs from your AI assistant, then save the ones
worth pursuing. freehire now uses one hosted MCP address for public search and
personal tools:

```text
https://freehire.me/api/v1/mcp
```

You can ask your assistant for remote Go jobs, look up an employer or compare
salary ranges without signing in. When you want to save a shortlist or read your
tracked jobs, connect your freehire account through OAuth. The server address
stays the same.

Previously, setup asked you to choose between a public connector and a separate
account connector. That choice made a simple request awkward: find some jobs,
then save the ones worth pursuing. A single connection now supports both parts.

The [catalogue snapshot](https://freehire.me/api/v1/stats/catalog) on 5 November
2026 contains 4,990,891 unique open jobs, 684,916 company profiles, 437 sources
and 178 ATS platforms. These are catalogue figures, not a promise that every
company currently has an open role.

## Search first, connect your account when you need it

Public tools search jobs and employers, read postings, check recorded posting
availability and return salary and hiring statistics. They need no freehire
account or API key.

After you approve OAuth access, your assistant can read your profile and tracking
board, save jobs, update application stages and manage job alerts. Those changes
appear in the same account you use on the website. You can revoke the connection
from **Connected devices** in your account.

For example, start with:

> Find remote backend Go roles in Europe.

Then ask:

> Save the best three to my board.

Your assistant needs account access for the second request. If it does not open
sign-in automatically, use its authentication control. You keep the same server.

## The same address in Claude, ChatGPT and coding agents

The [MCP setup guide](/mcp) has instructions for each assistant. For Claude Code:

```sh
claude mcp add --transport http freehire https://freehire.me/api/v1/mcp
```

When you want personal tools, run `claude mcp login freehire`. In Codex, add the
same URL with `codex mcp add freehire --url https://freehire.me/api/v1/mcp`, then
run `codex mcp login freehire` to connect your account. Approve access in your
browser. You do not need to copy a token into the configuration.

ChatGPT supports public search and account access through the same Freehire
connection. Tool availability in a directory listing also depends on the
provider's review. The guide includes custom-connection instructions.

## Tracking and sending an application are different actions

Saving a job or marking it applied changes your tracking board. Neither action
sends anything to an employer.

For automatic applications, connect with OAuth and enable **Let connected agents
apply for me** under **Account → Integrations → API keys**. Then explicitly ask
your assistant to prepare an application on a supported employer form. You review
the prepared application before approving submission. This workflow is subject to
your plan and allowance.

The account tools also let an agent suggest a missing skill, specialization or
industry for the dictionary, and report a failed operation. An empty search alone
is not evidence that a dictionary term is missing. Problem reports should omit
secrets and personal documents.

**Update, 13 November 2026:** the hosted MCP now requires sign-in for every tool,
search included, because Claude.ai and other assistants only offer sign-in when a
server asks for it on the first request. A connector saved with
the older `/api/v1/mcp/account` address keeps working; if it asks you to sign in
again, do.
